WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.200
TAKUTO KIRA

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.200
W-What are you doing?!

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.230
Takuto! Do you understand
what this means?

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.000
What the heck is fate anyway?
It's stupid.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.800
I'm not gonna let Mitsuki die.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.330
There's no way a half-baked guy like
you could do something like that alone!

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.230
Meroko! You...

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:24.400
Yeah!

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:25.530
TAKUTO KIRA
MEROKO YUI
Me too.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.230
Live?

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.760
That's the title that I want to use.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.460
You're using it to mean "to live"
as well as a "live concert" huh?

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:19.500
Yes.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.160
I think it's a good idea.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:26.630
Actually, I just used the word that
Takuto gave me the other day.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.560
Well...if I could possibly...

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.930
What is it? Just tell us.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.100
I would like to have
my live concert on that day.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.460
The day I met Meroko and Takuto
for the first time.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.000
My...well...

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:43.660
My last day!

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.730
Well, that's also the day
that I have a surgery.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.260
Well...

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.930
Can we not do that?

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.500
I guess I am
supposed to say "no."

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.130
But we can work something out.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:03.730
Like, we can finish the check-ups
the day before.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:05.460
Are you sure?

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:06.260
Yes.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.800
Thank you very much!

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.930
See, you never know until you ask!

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:11.760
Yeah.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.730
Sorry, Keichi.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.030
No worries.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.800
Okay, we need to get started now.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:22.360
We have to reserve the site,
prepare ads, and promote to the media.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:26.560
Mitsuki's concert...
We'll definitely make a hit!

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.030
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.060
It'll be a pretty big stage, huh?

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:46.130
Okay, I'll do my best on the ads!

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.230
Thank you very much!

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.130
Thank you.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:55.360
Anyways, it's hard to believe it's been
a year since you debuted. Time flies!

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.460
Thank you very much for everything.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.460
I remember the first time we met very well.
Shrimp pilaf.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.660
I was so surprised about that!

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.000
I'm sorry about that.
I answered like a little girl.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:12.100
No, no, it was actually refreshing.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.430
Since your comments were so interesting,
I just used them the way they were.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.560
- What's wrong?
- But readers seemed to

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.960
- Nothing.
- like them very much.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:25.460
I'm sorry, it was her first job,
so she was quite nervous.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.400
Yes, that's right.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:30.400
Huh?

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.030
M-Mr. Takeda, are you okay?

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:49.060
Don't worry!
I just made him fall asleep.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:54.330
I-I see. But why did Full Moon
transform back into Mitsuki?

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:55.500
Takuto?

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:56.800
Sorry, sorry.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.430
Hey! Come on!
Hey! Hey! Hey!

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.060
What's wrong?

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:09.930
Well...

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:13.700
Hurry, Takuto!

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:16.060
I know! Go!

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:32.360
Oops! I'm sorry I fell asleep!
I must be exhausted.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.760
P-Please don't worry!

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.200
Huh? Since when was
this stuffed animal here?

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.630
What are you talking about, Mr. Takeda?
It's been there since we got here!

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:46.330
Really?!

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.160
Y-Yes, it's my favorite
stuffed animal.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.300
I bring it with me everywhere I go.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:51.800
Oh, I see.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.660
- Yes, that's right!
- That's right!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.760
Oh, Mr. Takeda!

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:12.260
Takuto...
I hope he's okay.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.160
Yeah.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.100
What?

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:17.330
I'm not putting on a show!

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:19.730
I-I'm sorry!

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:26.030
Don't worry about what happened today!
I was just a little tired.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:28.600
Really?

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.160
You don't believe me?

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.800
It's not that I don't believe you, but...

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:35.630
Okay, watch me!

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.930
Let this withered tree bloom!

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.200
Wow!

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:49.600
See, I told you!

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:09.830
H-Hey, Takuto.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.030
Don't' say anything!

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:20.330
Takuto!

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:24.730
Takuto, are you okay? Takuto!

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:26.700
I-I'm okay.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.830
No, you're not!

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.500
Takuto... Could it be...

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.930
<i>It's the same as before.</i>

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:50.430
<i>I thought you had stopped turning</i>
<i>into a ghost, but were we wrong?</i>

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.260
It's my fault.
It's my fault!

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.260
No, it's not!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.430
It has nothing to do with you.

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:08.060
This is my problem.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.500
No! I don't want you
to become a ghost!

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:12.430
Don't cry!

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.300
You too, Mitsuki.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:19.230
But...

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:21.760
Just calm down.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:32.660
Takuto!

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.660
I guess I'm okay now.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:37.360
Don't worry about me
becoming a ghost.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.930
It's not like I wanted to be
a Death Spirit either.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.760
Plus, I don't wanna stay
a Death Spirit forever anyways.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:46.300
Takuto...

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.200
More importantly, the problem is
Mitsuki's transformation.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:56.230
The reason why Mitsuki can transform
is because she's got my blood in her.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:59.960
So she can transform
as long as I exist.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.460
If I became a ghost...

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:09.030
In other words,
if I disappear,

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:13.160
Mitsuki will never be able to
transform into Full Moon ever again.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.100
Shoot! All this with the important
concert coming up!

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.060
The concert is not
the problem for you!

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:24.860
That's right!
We can't let you become a ghost!

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:25.900
Yes. Let's—

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:26.930
Just listen to me!

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:30.600
Please listen to me.

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:37.760
I may not be perfect as either
a human or a Death Spirit,

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.600
but I always try to
keep a promise.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.660
Do you remember our promise?

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:44.500
Our promise?

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.130
<i>I guess there's</i>
<i>no way around it.</i>

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:54.430
<i>Go as far as you can with it.</i>
<i>I'll help you with your dream for one year.</i>

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.000
<i>Are you sure?</i>

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:05.630
Yeah.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.330
The day of your concert will be
the last day for our promise.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.060
I will keep our promise!

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:16.800
I'll be sure to let you transform!

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:24.600
There shouldn't be any problem!
We've always managed, right?

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:25.960
Am I wrong?

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:28.530
I guess so.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:30.660
You're right.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:32.100
That is right.

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:34.460
Okay, we'll have to do
something about it.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.460
I'll think about something
for the worst-case scenario.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:39.160
You're thinking about
the worst-case scenario already?

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:43.600
And my Death Spirit power
might still be okay too.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:45.260
Right.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.030
All right, I'll do my best too!

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.260
That's good! That's the spirit!

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:56.400
Me too!

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:57.260
Yeah!

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:58.930
Let's do it!

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:10.160
What's up?

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:13.660
Do you think we should tell
Ms. Oshige about this?

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:15.600
Not tonight.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:19.630
If the situation with my powers
is the same tomorrow morning,

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:21.100
we can tell her then.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.960
I hope your powers
will be back to normal.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:25.930
Yeah.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.200
<i>Aoi, don't worry.</i>

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.100
<i>I'll complete the mission.</i>

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:32.530
See, I told you that I'd be fine.

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:43.330
It didn't work.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:45.230
Don't be disappointed like that.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.800
It's only been a day.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.400
Takuto, drink this.

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:56.260
What is it?

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.530
It's an energy drink.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:58.430
Huh?

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:01.030
What do I have to
perk myself up for?

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.630
Well, why don't you
go ahead and have it,

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:05.800
since she picked it up for you.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.130
Oh fine.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:14.130
Do these really work?

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:20.800
H-How was it?

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.430
It seems like it's
not working for him.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:30.130
Yeah.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:31.660
I know!

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.800
Yes! What do you think?

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:42.130
You think I can become Full Moon
with some make-up?

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:52.030
I should call Ms. Oshige after all,
and ask her to cancel the photo shoot.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:54.630
I got an idea!

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:04.760
Good, good! That's good!
Keep doing that!

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.500
Meroko is doing a pretty good job!

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:12.930
I was worried because things don't go well
when she's enthusiastic about something,

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.000
but I guess she knows you well.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:18.330
Full Moon, bring your face
up right there.

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:19.400
Yes.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.060
Stare into the distance.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.560
Yeah, good.
That's right.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:31.460
<i>Who is Full Moon?</i>

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:40.360
<i>It's me, but it's not me.</i>

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.960
<i>Before I became Full Moon,</i>

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:48.900
<i>I was a girl who didn't have any friends</i>
<i>and dreamed of becoming a singer.</i>

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.530
<i>I made friends.</i>

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:32.700
<i>A lot of friends!</i>

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:39.100
<i>It's all thanks to Full Moon.</i>

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.700
W-What?
What's wrong, Mitsuki?

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:53.560
I truly thank you, Takuto.
That you let me transform into Full Moon.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:54.530
What?

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:59.700
You've let me experience many things
that Mitsuki Koyama could never have.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.930
Thank you very much.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.260
What's up with you
all of the sudden?

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:11.560
I don't know. I just wanted to thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:16.600
Are you okay, Mitsuki?

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.100
I'm...fine.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.030
Are you sure?
But just in case...

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.830
It's not getting worse
so you should be okay.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:30.230
Great!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.560
Thank you very much.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.530
Umm... About Takuto...

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:42.660
Yeah, about that.
He has to take it easy and rest.

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.460
I'm fine. I know about myself
more than anyone else.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.600
Meroko, please take care of Takuto.

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:51.330
Uh-oh!

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:52.160
Yes!

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:57.060
If he tries to do something rash,
please stop him no matter what.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.630
Sure, I will.

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:18.700
Meroko...

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:22.730
I'll take care of Takuto,
so you go to bed, Mitsuki.

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:23.430
But...

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:25.930
Don't make me
take care of you as well.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:27.460
Y-Yeah.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:52.030
<i>I shouldn't be crying.</i>
<i>This is no time to cry.</i>

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.230
<i>I can't cry.</i>

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:57.130
Takuto, hang in there.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:30.860
<i>Meroko and Takuto are</i>
<i>doing the best they can do.</i>

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:35.360
<i>Isn't there anything that I can do?</i>

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:40.560
Wow, I found something good!

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:43.130
I will show it to Izumi.

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:51.030
<i>Those two might know</i>
<i>how to help Takuto.</i>

00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:59.600
Izumi!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.760
Hey, hey, Izumi, look at this.

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:05.360
Does it look good on me?

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:07.730
You're so annoying.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:15.030
Izumi, are you still thinking about
that middle-aged woman by any chance?

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.230
It's none of your business,
Jonathan.

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:22.800
She probably doesn't like you anymore.
Oh, poor thing, Izumi! Poor thing!

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:25.830
- Shut up.
- Poor thing, poor thing, poor thing!

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:27.360
In English, that would be...

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:29.930
Oh, we have a guest!

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.760
A stranger's here,
a stranger's here.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:38.730
Oh my, you came all the way here
to visit me, Mikki?

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:58.530
I want you to tell me if you know.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:02.560
Do you know how to prevent
Takuto from turning into a ghost?

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:05.530
Yes, I do.

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:07.160
Really?

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:11.660
Please tell me! Please!

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:16.730
I can tell you, but...
Can I give you one condition?

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.700
Y-Yes.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:23.530
Your soul.

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:27.400
Can I take your soul?

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:28.360
What?

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:32.300
So what's it gonna be, Mikki?

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:38.760
<i>I don't wanna die because I finally</i>
<i>feel like I have to live...that I want to live.</i>

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.300
<i>But...</i>

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:46.330
<i>I don't wanna lose Takuto</i>
<i>after I lost Eichi!</i>

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:54.630
<i>Takuto... He'd get get mad at me.</i>
<i>But I don't ever wanna feel that way!</i>

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.430
Okay, as long as
we can save Takuto!

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:04.260
Well then...

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:24.430
Well, to seal our contract, Mikki,
I will have you kiss me.

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:08.360
Mitsuki, you're being rash!

00:23:08.460 --> 00:23:12.600
I know you want to save Takuto,
but you shouldn't have gone to Izumi!

00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:15.400
No, it's what I needed
to do to save Takuto.

00:23:15.430 --> 00:23:16.760
I don't care what happens to me.

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:18.160
Mitsuki...

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:24.200
Gosh, Takuto, pull yourself together!
I won't accept you disappearing!

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:30.230
Next time on Full Moon:
"Mitsuki's Feelings, Meroko's Feelings."

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:31.960
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
